---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import exploring from '../assets/img/exploring.jpg';

import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Paragraph from '../components/ui/Paragraph.astro';
import PortfolioLayout from '../templates/PortfolioLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
import Link from '../components/ui/Link.astro';
---

<PortfolioLayout
  title="About · Nathaniel Hernandez"
  description="How a ten-year-old with Photoshop became a frontend developer and UX designer in Boston."
>
  <Hero title="About" headingLevel={1}>
    <Paragraph>Let's get to know each other.</Paragraph>
  </Hero>
  <Section title="The TL;DR version">
    <!-- prettier-ignore -->
    <Paragraph size="xs" lineHeight="lg">
      I'm a developer and designer based in Boston, Massachusetts. My passion is
      creating beautiful, accessible interfaces that are a joy to both look at
      and use. I'd love to hear from you. Email me at
      <Link href="mailto:hello@nathanielhernandez.me">
        hello@nathanielhernandez.me
      </Link>.
    </Paragraph>
  </Section>
  <Section title="The full story">
    <Image
      src={exploring}
      alt="Nathaniel standing on the crest of a sand dune under a cloudy sky"
      layout="constrained"
      width={768}

      position="bottom"
      quality={'high'}
      class="aboutPhoto"
    />
    <Paragraph size="xs" lineHeight="lg">
      I first opened Photoshop at ten years old, which sparked my passion for
      graphic design. I spent my early years designing logos for small
      businesses and building mock brand identities for fun.
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph size="xs" lineHeight="lg">
      Around the age of thirteen, I discovered I could combine design with web
      development using HTML and CSS. It perfectly scratched the creative and
      technical itch I'd always had. I felt confident in my ability to design
      but wanted to strengthen my technical knowledge, so I decided to pursue a
      degree in Computer Science at Boise State University.
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph size="xs" lineHeight="lg">
      After graduating, I joined a local company that offered a path into UI/UX
      design. I took it, and that path led to where I am now: a frontend
      developer and UX designer who gets to do both every day.
    </Paragraph>
  </Section>
</PortfolioLayout>

<style>
  .aboutPhoto {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 768 / 468;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: bottom;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {
    .aboutPhoto {
      aspect-ratio: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
